    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "A good research question is narrow enough to be answered completely. Your RQ is very open, and the Sub-RQs only partially answer it, and broaden your scope even more. Focus on a clear and concrete research questions, with Sub-questions that address a specific part of your RQ."
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "The methodology presented should make clear how the RQs will be answered. Even though you present a high level of detail in your methodology, the methods don't seem to be linked to your RQs and are as such mostly irrelevant - for example the AI platform has not even been mentioned in your RQs. Either adjust your RQs to align with your actual research goal, or you tailor your methods towards the RQs. This is a really important point for a good expose!"
